win32: render GL through ANGLE into a composition swapchain

WGL renders into a child window that DirectComposition shows without alpha,
so the transparent shadow margin of client-side decorated windows and
popovers turns black. The Vulkan path only keeps alpha when the driver offers
a premultiplied swapchain.

With Direct Composition on and ANGLE available, GDK now initializes EGL on
ANGLE using the display's own D3D11 device. Each surface renders into a pbuffer
wrapping the back buffer of a composition swapchain with premultiplied alpha,
which becomes the content of the surface's visual. A Y flip on the visual
corrects GL's bottom-up rows. Without ANGLE, WGL is used as before.

Also fixes the order of the overloaded IDCompositionVisual methods in dcomp.h,
which put SetTransform (matrix) in the slot of SetTransform (object).

